
Question 1: Exploring The Course Management System (CMS)

Q1. How many entity classes are there in the schema (org.example.schema.CMS.*)?
    There are 5 entity classes in the schema. These are the course class, the professor class,
    the student class, the teaches class, and the transcript class.

Q2. What purpose does the cms-ddl.sql file serve? Where is it used?
    The cms-ddl.sql file defines the database schema for the course management system where 
    the data from the course, professor, student, teaches, and transcript csv files will be 
    stored. The system reads this file and uses it to set up constraints, such as data types, 
    primary keys, and foreign key constraints before any data is actually loaded into the
    tables.

Q3. What are the foreign keys of the transcript table?
    The foreign keys of the transcript table are studentId, which is referenced from the
    student table, and courseId, which is referenced from the course table.

Q4. How many parameters does the FindStudent query have?
    The FindStudent query only has one parameter, which is :studentId.

Q5. What format is the database stored in?
    The database is an in memory DuckDB database, and its data is stored in CSV files 
    that get loaded in when the program runs.

